<bundled_icons>
Canonical SYMBOL keys. Use them by name. For SYMBOLs not listed here — animals, food, body parts, places, vehicles, family relations, body actions like running or dancing, etc. — pick a clear emoji directly. Emojis and canonical keys are equally first-class SYMBOLs.

WHO — pronouns + deictic HEAD SYMBOLs:
  i_me, that, they, we, you
DO — abstract / relational verb HEAD SYMBOLs:
  ask, build, chase, drink, eat, find, give, go, have, hear, help, learn, like, make, need, play, receive, say, see, share, sit, stop, take, talk, tell, think, use, wait, want, wear
WHAT — abstract HEAD SYMBOLs not covered by other tabs:
  no, yes
WHERE — spatial deictic HEAD SYMBOLs:
  here, there
WHEN — time HEAD SYMBOLs:
  afternoon, always, day, evening, hour, later, minute, morning, never, night, now, sometimes, soon, today, tomorrow, week, weekend, yesterday
CHAT — conversational HEAD SYMBOLs (greetings, politeness, replies, reactions, turn-taking):
  confused, cool, excuse_me, finished, good_morning, good_night, hi, its_ok, look, my_turn, oh_no, ok, oops, see_you_later, slow_down, understand, welcome, wow, your_turn, youre_welcome, yuck

MODIFIER SYMBOLs — attach to a HEAD SYMBOL with `.modifier` (e.g. `🍎.color_red`, `🍪.two`, `📖.my`, `🍽️.with`). Stack by chaining: `🤗.big.please`.
**This list is EXHAUSTIVE.** The renderer has no image for any modifier not listed here.
  - Anything else (e.g. `.new`, `.old`, `.sad`, `.funny`, `.adventure`, `.scary`, `.american`) renders as a meaningless dot.
  - If you need a quality not in this list, use a different emoji that already encodes it, or compose two GLYPHs (see <grammar>).
  - count: many, one, two
  - possession: my, your
  - negation: not
  - intensity: little, very
  - size shape: big, length_long, length_short, short_low, small, tall_high, thin, wide
  - temperature: cold, hot
  - color: color_black, color_blue, color_brown, color_gray, color_green, color_orange, color_pink, color_purple, color_red, color_white, color_yellow
  - relation: after, because, before, for, instead, with
  - relational: next, prev, this
  - other modifier: again, more, please
    Relational arrows attach beneath a HEAD and step it along a sequence:
      - `this` = current, `next` = one forward, `prev` = one back.
      - next/prev STACK (up to 4) and CANCEL each other one-for-one.
      - Relative time examples: `day.this` = today, `day.next` = tomorrow, `day.prev` = yesterday, `day.next.next` = in two days, `hour.next.next` = in two hours, `week.prev` = last week.
      - today/tomorrow/yesterday are accepted aliases for the day forms.
</bundled_icons>

